Anvil Browser license
=====================

Copyright (c) 2026 Buntos

Two licenses apply:

- All rights reserved for the browser, network, and sandbox crates (`LICENSE-PROPRIETARY`)
- MPL-2.0 for the sibling libraries (`LICENSE-MPL`)

The page engine is not in this repository. `anvil-dom`, `anvil-style`,
`anvil-layout`, `anvil-paint`, `anvil-raster`, and `anvil-script` are
the separate repository `anvil-engine`. This file does not license them.
Revisions of those crates that were already published in this repository
under the Apache License 2.0 stay under that license for those revisions
only.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART II: HARDCODED SECURITY, SANDBOX, SHIELD & APPLICATION TIER
         (Proprietary — All Rights Reserved)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Applies to:
- `crates/anvil-sandbox` (Mandatory OS process isolation & job-object guard)
- `crates/anvil-net` (Pre-Socket Tracker/Ad/Malware Shield, HSTS, FIPS 180-4
  SHA-256 Subresource Integrity, CSP, CORP, RFC 6265bis CookieJar, & TLS)
- `crates/anvil-browser` (Windows DPAPI and Linux AES-256-GCM `profile.anvil` encryption, SHA-256
  Download Verifier & Quarantine, UI shell, installer, and `anvil.exe` /
  `AnvilBrowser-Setup` compiled binaries)
- `frontend/` (Privileged React/TSX and JavaScript browser shell & pages:
  `App.tsx`, `components/*.tsx`, `scripts/*.js`, and `styles/browser.css`)
- `assets/anvil-mark.png` (Official Anvil Browser brand mark)

See `LICENSE-PROPRIETARY` for full terms:
1. Ownership: All files, security policies, cryptographic containers, front-end
   UI components, brand assets, and compiled binaries in Part II are the sole
   and exclusive proprietary property of Buntos. All Rights Reserved.
2. Source-Available Audit Only: While the Part II source files are published
   in this repository for transparency and security verification, no license
   or right is granted to copy, modify, redistribute, rebrand, fork,
   sublicense, or create derivative or commercial works from any Part II
   component without prior written permission from Buntos.

